fset\u001b[38;5;252m and returns HistoryAction with\u001b[13;38H  render_history=\u001b[38;5;179mTrue\u001b[38;5;252m and forwarded_input=\u001b[38;5;179mb\"\"\u001b[38;5;252m — no upstream input.\u001b[14;38H  3. apply_history_action only sends upstream when \u001b[38;5;110maction.forwarded_input\u001b[38;5;252m is set; empty means nothing reaches tmux. The overlay is painted\u001b[15;38H  client-side via \u001b[38;5;110msurface.paint_overlays\u001b[38;5;252m.\u001b[16;38H  4. This is a fast-client history overlay over bounded snapshots, not tmux copy-mode; the implementation notes stock tmux WheelUpPane would\u001b[17;38H  enter copy-mode, which is deliberately avoided.\u001b[18;38H  Focused test: \u001b[38;5;114mtests/test_fast_display_history.py::test_local_history_routes_sidebar_immediately_and_owns_agent_wheel\u001b[38;5;252m asserts\u001b[19;38H  \u001b[38;5;110magent_action.forwarded_input\u001b[38;5;252m \u001b[38;5;179m==\u001b[38;5;252m \u001b[38;5;179mb\"\"\u001b[38;5;252m.\u001b[20;38H  Suggested addition: assert \u001b[38;5;110magent_action.render_history\u001b[38;5;252m is \u001b[38;5;179mTrue\u001b[38;5;252m, proving the overlay rendered rather than merely dropping the event.\u001b[34;38H\u001b[38;5;239m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[35;38H\u001b[38;5;147m❯\u001b[39m \u001b[36;38H\u001b[38;5;239m────"]
